sequenceDiagram
  %% route.update on the Gateway engine: a `--domain` change of route/update.mmd (workflow operation-route-update) built from route.create's primitives and route/engine/destroy.mmd's withdrawal. Design for ADR 0267 and ADR 0271; no engine flow exists yet. Step names describe effects; the implementation settles action names unless an existing action is named.
  %% No primitive is new here: `tls.ensure_csr`, `route.publish_site` and `dns.publish_records` exist (docs/reference/gateway-engine.md#routecreate); the old site's withdrawal and the DNS grace are those of route/engine/destroy.mmd.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: route:update
  %% kind: route.update
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane EN icon=workflow pill=engine tone=purple
  %% lane N icon=server pill=executor tone=amber
  %% lane V icon=server pill=executor tone=green
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant EN as Engine<br/>Gateway and NATS
  participant N as Route Node<br/>executor
  participant V as VPN Node<br/>DNS executor
  CLI->>GW: route:update ROUTE<br/>at least one option
  Note over GW: Validate, lock, record<br/>replacement pending
  %%> Same validation as route/update.mmd
  alt nothing to do on a Node
    GW-->>CLI: 200 OK<br/>nothing to change
    %%> No Operation, no engine decision
  else Node work needed
    Note over GW: Hold the Route Nodes
    alt the engine admits the whole Operation
      %%> Admission, one decision per Operation (EngineKinds::routes):
      %%> - `route.update` is in `ORBIT_ENGINE_KINDS`
      %%> - every Node a step touches reports its action in `$KV.NODES`: `tls.ensure_csr`, `route.publish_site` and the site withdrawal on each Route Node, `dns.publish_records` on each VPN Node
      %%> - the flow accepts the plan shape; a part it does not cover throws `EngineUnsupported` before any order
      %%> - eligible plan: `--domain` on a private Route; `--publication`, a public Route's domain change (Ingress edge, ufw 80/443) and LAN rules throw `EngineUnsupported`
      Note over GW: Bind steps, take the lock<br/>commit, publish the start
      %%> - the step rows and the Operation lock commit in one transaction before the start event; an Operation never moves between engines after this
      GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
      EN->>N: Make the key and CSR<br/>tls.ensure_csr · csr-i
      %%> The key is made once and never leaves the Node; a resend answers a request for the same key
      N-->>EN: CSR<br/>output
      Note over EN: Sign the CSR<br/>Gateway step · sign-i
      %%> `operation:direct:certificate-sign`; the Orbit CA key stays in the Gateway; a pending cancel refuses
      EN->>N: Publish the new site<br/>route.publish_site · site-node
      %%> Leaf, Caddy site, PHP-FPM pool and `APP_URL` of a Laravel target, as route.create; validated before the move, reload only on change
      N-->>EN: Files placed<br/>applied
      EN->>N: Probe the site over TLS<br/>Gateway step · SNI new domain
      opt domain outside the TLD
        EN->>V: Move the DNS answers<br/>dns.publish_records · dns-i
        %%> Records and catalog with the new name and without the old one, with the admitted digest, as route/engine/destroy.mmd
        V-->>EN: Files and restart<br/>applied
        Note over EN: Wait the DNS grace<br/>31 s: TTL 30 s + 1 s
        %%> Clients still resolving the old name keep it until their answer expires; the old site serves until then
      end
      opt a lasting site is replaced
        EN->>N: Withdraw the old site<br/>route family · withdraw-node
        %%> The primitive of route/engine/destroy.mmd, with the old domain's captured states; it never touches the new site
        N-->>EN: Old site absent<br/>read back
      end
      opt the receipt is lost
        EN->>N: Resend the same step<br/>fresh nonce · same step ID
        %%> When:
        %%> - the step passes its resend deadline with no receipt; two sends, one execution
        %%> - the Operation keeps its lock, so the Route and its held Nodes stays fenced; no other Operation and no Swamp run acts on it meanwhile
        %%> On the Node:
        %%> - the journal holds `done` for this Operation step, action and target: the executor answers the stored result with `repeat: true` and does not act again
        %%> - an order still `open` replays under the target lock first; an order that expired before the lock did nothing (`executor.order_expired`), and the step is sent again
        N-->>EN: Stored result<br/>repeat: true
      end
      alt every step verified
        EN->>GW: Record replacement active<br/>free the held Nodes
        %%> - the kind's own projection records the result, the same rows a Swamp run records
      else a step fails
        EN--xGW: Failed step<br/>error_code · redacted detail
        %%> - a deterministic refusal is a terminal receipt too; the journal keeps it and a resend repeats it
        Note over GW: Mark the change failed<br/>rerun resumes
        %%> - each step converges on a rerun: a made key is reused, a published site and DNS files repeat with `applied: 0`
      end
    else the engine does not admit it
      Note over GW: Start the Swamp run<br/>operation-route-update
      %%> - the kind is not enabled, a Node lacks the action, `$KV.NODES` is unreadable, or the flow throws `EngineUnsupported`: the whole Operation runs operation-route-update (route/update.mmd)
      %%> - no step of it runs on the engine; an Operation never splits across engines
    end
    loop every 2 s until terminal
      CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
      GW-->>CLI: status + result
    end
  end
